\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Distributional comparison of generated and real plasmids across length (kb), GC content (\%), and ViennaRNA MFE density (kcal/mol/nt). Three populations per panel: real held-out Addgene ($n{=}500$), supervised base ($n{=}1{,}000$), and post-GRPO ($n{=}1{,}000$). Inner box shows IQR and median; the dotted reference line is the real-population median; means are printed under each panel. The GC panel shows the headline distributional failure mode: a long low-GC tail in the supervised base, driven by a subpopulation of near-all-AT outputs, that post-training truncates and replaces with a real-like distribution.}}{8}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:distributions}{{4}{8}{Distributional comparison of generated and real plasmids across length (kb), GC content (\%), and ViennaRNA MFE density (kcal/mol/nt). Three populations per panel: real held-out Addgene ($n{=}500$), supervised base ($n{=}1{,}000$), and post-GRPO ($n{=}1{,}000$). Inner box shows IQR and median; the dotted reference line is the real-population median; means are printed under each panel. The GC panel shows the headline distributional failure mode: a long low-GC tail in the supervised base, driven by a subpopulation of near-all-AT outputs, that post-training truncates and replaces with a real-like distribution}{figure.caption.7}{}}
